> What I mean is that because the empty string is grammatical, a text will
> be discovered for any input, whether or not the input is grammatical and
> can be consumed. This is easy enough to correct for. What's proving to be a
> more difficult obstacle in using the parser to detect lojban texts is the
> "bare cmevla" rule: "lojban is an improved version of loglan" parses as a
> grammatical bare cmevla sequence. But that's a whole 'nother kettle of
> fish.
>

Yes, but it's not just cmevla. What about "mi casa es su casa", or "my dog
never liked tiramisu, but I do"?

